{
  "_note": [
    "A SYNTHETIC Management API answer for scripts/check-deploy.mjs --target hosted, NOT a recording.",
    "No hosted Supabase project exists for this product (E7 design's boundary paragraph; docs/CURRENT.md), so this",
    "lane made no hosted call and could record nothing. The field names below are modelled on Supabase's documented",
    "Management API shapes for GET /v1/projects/{ref}/config/auth, /postgrest and /database/migrations, and they are",
    "UNVERIFIED against a live answer. That is a real limitation and it is written here rather than implied: the",
    "first hosted run of the check is also the first check of these names, and a name that turns out to be different",
    "makes its rule report UNREAD, never a false pass, because every rule reads a named field and reports unread",
    "when it is absent (case E7-23's last arm asserts exactly that).",
    "The values are a project configured the way the hosted checklist requires, so the whole file is the clean",
    "control and each of E7-18's cases changes exactly one field of it."
  ],
  "auth": {
    "site_url": "https://enterprise.example.invalid",
    "disable_signup": true,
    "mailer_autoconfirm": false,
    "hook_before_user_created_enabled": true,
    "hook_before_user_created_uri": "pg-functions://postgres/app/hook_before_user_created",
    "hook_mfa_verification_attempt_enabled": true,
    "hook_mfa_verification_attempt_uri": "pg-functions://postgres/app/hook_mfa_verification_attempt",
    "mfa_totp_enroll_enabled": true,
    "mfa_totp_verify_enabled": true,
    "refresh_token_rotation_enabled": true,
    "security_refresh_token_reuse_interval": 0,
    "mailer_templates_magic_link_content": "<!--\n  GoTrue's own sign-in mail, the one message this product does not send itself (E7 design 1.1 and 2.2; E2 pages design\n  lines 421 to 430). A returning member asks for a link on /signin/, the server calls GoTrue's /otp, and GoTrue sends\n  this template through the project's SMTP settings.\n\n  WHAT THE LINK MUST BE, and it is the whole reason this file exists. The secret travels in the URL FRAGMENT, which no\n  browser sends to any server, so it stays out of Netlify's edge and request logs, out of any proxy and out of a\n  Referer: <site>/signin/#token_hash=<hash>&type=magiclink. GoTrue's default template sends {{ .ConfirmationURL }}\n  instead, which is a GoTrue /verify URL carrying the token in the QUERY STRING and following a redirect; this product\n  never uses it. {{ .TokenHash }} is the same value the accept link carries, and /signin/ posts it to\n  /api/auth/verify, where the server exchanges it for the session cookies.\n\n  HOW IT IS INSTALLED, and what proves it. This file is the source of truth; a person pastes its body into the hosted\n  project's Magic Link template by hand (E7 1.4 D13 compares the hosted content's SHA-256 with this file's, and H-A12\n  and H-M4 record the observation that the mail arrives and lands on /signin/). NOTHING LOCAL PROVES ANY OF IT: the\n  local stack has no SMTP configured, so GoTrue's mailer is a no-op and no message is ever delivered (E2 section 11).\n  The local suites therefore never read this file, and a change to it is proven only by the hosted receipt.\n\n  WHAT IT MAY CONTAIN: the link, the site's name, and fixed sentences. It carries no customer content, no company\n  name, no tracking pixel, no image, no external stylesheet and no link but the one below; {{ .Email }} is deliberately\n  not printed, because the mail is already in that mailbox.\n\n  WHO IT REACHES, after E7-28: an account that has already been confirmed. GoTrue v2.192.0 refuses the sign-in start\n  for an account that is still unconfirmed, which every first-time invitee's is, so a first-time invitee never receives\n  this mail and is served by the invitation mail and, past its hour, by a new invitation (evidence/e7-mail.md).\n-->\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <title>Your sign-in link for Phaeacia</title>\n  </head>\n  <body style=\"font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.5; color: #1a1a1a\">\n    <p>You asked to sign in to Phaeacia with this address.</p>\n    <p>\n      <a href=\"{{ .SiteURL }}/signin/#token_hash={{ .TokenHash }}&amp;type=magiclink\">Open this link to sign in.</a>\n    </p>\n    <p>The link works once, and for one hour. After that, ask for a new one on the sign-in page.</p>\n    <p>If you did not ask to sign in, ignore this mail. Nothing happens until the link is opened.</p>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  },
